	abstract = {As artificial intelligence (AI) continues to revolutionize manufacturing, the focus has shifted to ensuring the security, transparency, and reliability of these systems. Safeguarding AI-driven processes involves addressing challenges such as data integrity, system vulnerabilities, ethical considerations, and regulatory compliance to foster trust, innovation, and sustainable growth in AI-powered manufacturing environments. This review explores cutting-edge strategies to enhance security and foster trust within AI-assisted manufacturing environments. It focuses on integrating cybersecurity mechanisms with intelligent systems to prevent vulnerabilities and data breaches that may compromise operations. The study discusses advanced encryption algorithms, secure communication protocols, and robust authentication techniques as core pillars for building secure infrastructures. These components help safeguard sensitive production data, intellectual property, and system commands from malicious attacks or unauthorized access. In addition to technical security, the review emphasizes the need for ethical AI governance, including transparency, accountability, and explainability in decision-making. Such principles ensure that AI outputs can be verified and interpreted by human operators, building user confidence in automated processes. The incorporation of real-time monitoring systems and anomaly detection tools further strengthens the resilience of AI systems against evolving cyber threats and operational disruptions. It also offers a forward-looking viewpoint on how to include cross-disciplinary policies, ethical AI legislation, and adaptive cybersecurity frameworks to guarantee the long-term resilience and sustainability of AI-powered industrial ecosystems. It highlights the emerging role of blockchain technologies in manufacturing. Blockchain supports decentralized data management, ensures traceability, and enables tamper-proof audit trails. Use cases involving smart contracts are examined to demonstrate how automated compliance and operational efficiency can be achieved. Through simulations and real-world applications, the study shows improvements in system reliability, productivity, and user trust. © 2025, Malque Publishing. All rights reserved.},
