	abstract = {The rapid spread of information and communication technologies (ICT) has among other things contributed to the outbreak of the basic need for social networking by means of electronic tools even in previously uninfected parts of the population. The creation of intelligent environments can be seen as one of the foundations on the basis of which "almost unlimited access to information (data) and other people"is made possible. The usage of artificial intelligence (AI) technology in wireless communications has recently gained a lot of interest. AI has shown real progress in the fields of voice comprehension, image recognition, and natural language processing, demonstrating the enormous ability in addressing challenges that cannot be conveniently modeled. AI strategies have been a crucial enabler in wireless communication, helping to satisfy the rising and varied demands through a broad variety of application scenarios. Due to the huge importance of the Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for the user interface, reliability, performance, and dynamic network conditions, the design and optimization of wireless communication networks are becoming increasingly difficult. AI may be used to solve difficult and historically intractable issues by learning from the observed world and leveraging the exponentially large databases available from wireless networks. Many challenges in wireless communication networks, such as decision making, resource optimization, and network control, may be conceived in a way that AI techniques can overcome. Based on this finding, it is important to explore where and how AI technologies may be used to enhance the efficiency of potential wireless communication systems. © 2025 Author(s).},
