	affiliations = {University of Technology, Sydney, Australia},
	abstract = {Artificial Intelligence (AI) is increasingly being leveraged into strategic decisionmaking processes across multinational companies, reshaping global industries. The rapid development and adoption led by multinational companies raises various questions on the actual capabilities and limitations of AI, what specific tasks can effectively be improved and associated risks to consider. This chapter focuses on the impacts of AI on global industries through a comparative case study examining four multinational corporations, comparing their unique implementation of AI across five criteria.The findings support the ability for AI to fundamentally address inherent decision-making challenges related to accuracy and timeliness of data, automation, while also highlighting areas sensitive to over-reliance on these automated processes. The conclusion provides a framework for businesses and policymakers to responsibly implement AI, including recommendations for improving AI governance, investing in employee upskilling, and ensuring ethical AI deployment to enhance long-term strategic outcomes. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
