	affiliations = {Shandong Key Laboratory of Ubiquitous Intelligent Computing, Jinan, 250022, China},
	abstract = {In the domain of automotive safety and intelligent transportation systems, abnormal driving behavior monitoring systems play an indispensable role in ensuring road safety. Current behavioral monitoring models face dual challenges of high-resolution image recognition requirements and significant latency in cloud deployment, resulting in suboptimal trade-offs between detection accuracy and resource consumption. To address these limitations, this study presents Light-YOLOv8n, an optimized target detection model specifically designed for abnormal driving scenarios through architectural enhancements to YOLOv8. Our technical contributions include: (1) Integration of channel attention mechanisms (SE Block) within the C2f module; (2) Implementation of a fully connected convolutional block attention module (CBAMByFC) in the backbone network. These structural modifications enable Light-YOLOv8n to maintain 99.0% of the original model's detection accuracy (mAP@0.5) while reducing parameter volume to 33.3% of the baseline YOLOv8. The lightweight architecture demonstrates efficient operation on low-power edge devices with minimal accuracy compromise. Our hardware implementation utilizing NanoPi NEO2 coupled with AI Compute Stick achieves 50% improvement in inference speed (0.1s vs. 0.2s original) and further reduces to 0.03s through model quantization techniques, representing 60% acceleration from pre-optimization levels. Experimental validation confirms stable average detection accuracy (98.2±0.3%) despite significant parameter reduction. Comparative analysis reveals Light-YOLOv8n's superior performance metrics (F1-score: 0.92, Precision: 94.5%, Recall: 89.7%) against current mainstream models, establishing new benchmarks in computational efficiency (23.4 GFLOPs) and practical deployment feasibility. This research advances intelligent transportation systems by providing an optimized technical framework that effectively balances detection performance with resource constraints in real-world driving monitoring applications  © COPYRIGHT SPIE. Downloading of the abstract is permitted for personal use only.},
