	affiliations = {Alagappa University, India},
	abstract = {This chapter explores how libraries are embarking on a transformative journey in the digital era, driven by the integration of artificial intelligence (AI). This technology is reshaping the library landscape and enhancing their ability to meet the evolving needs of users. Traditionally seen as repositories of knowledge and information, libraries are now leveraging AI to improve accessibility, streamline operations, and offer innovative services. This integration not only boosts the efficiency of library functions but also positions libraries as dynamic hubs for information discovery in the 21st century. In this discussion, we examine the various ways AI is influencing and reshaping the traditional roles of libraries, including enhancing information literacy and optimizing resource discovery. AI systems automate routine tasks, while AI technologies promote accessibility for a diverse range of users-including those with disabilities-by incorporating features like voice-activated controls and text-to-speech capabilities. Furthermore, AI-driven educational tools within libraries provide personalized learning experiences, tailoring content to match individual preferences and learning styles. However, the implementation of AI also raises ethical challenges concerning privacy, data security, and algorithmic biases, highlighting the importance of responsible AI practices. Libraries use AI-powered analytics to evaluate user behavior, preferences, and emerging trends, which informs their strategies for collection development and resource management. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
	keywords = {Artificial intelligence; Behavioral research; Data privacy; Digital libraries; Knowledge management; Learning systems; Artificial intelligence systems; Artificial intelligence technologies; Digital era; Diverse range; Information discovery; Information literacy; Library functions; Library services; Resource discovery; Streamline operations; Libraries},
