	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105016775029?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {Hoshin Kanri, or policy deployment, is a strategic decision-making methodology that aligns organizational goals with daily management activities to ensure long-term success. By integrating artificial intelligence (AI) into Hoshin Kanri, organizations can enhance strategic planning, optimize continuous improvement initiatives, and leverage predictive analytics for data-driven decision-making. AI-driven tools provide real-time insights, automate routine tasks, and improve the accuracy of forecasting, enabling organizations to refine their five-year vision, develop more precise one-year plans, and monitor progress with greater efficiency. However, the integration of AI into Hoshin Kanri also introduces critical data privacy and ethical considerations, including transparency in AI-driven decision-making, bias mitigation, regulatory compliance, and ethical data governance. This chapter explores the role of AI in enhancing Hoshin Kanri, the advantages of AI-driven strategic alignment, and the necessary safeguards to ensure responsible AI use. By embedding ethical AI principles into policy deployment, organizations can achieve a balanced approach that fosters continuous improvement, enhances accountability, and supports long-term resilience in an increasingly data-driven environment. © 2026 Adil Dalal and Elizabeth A. Cudney. All rights reserved.},
