	abstract = {Understanding and predicting near-miss accidents from dashcam footage is critical for intelligent transportation, yet conventional multimodal large language models (MLLMs) struggle with ambiguity, high computational demands, and hallucination in safety-critical contexts. We introduce a novel, lightweight neuro-symbolic AI framework that transforms video events into sequences of fixed-format symbolic templates (e.g., <action, object, direction, location, [intensity]>). Our transformer-based approach precisely aligns short video segments with these compact, human-readable templates and, crucially, predicts future templates to forecast events 0-5 seconds ahead—a vital capability for anticipatory risk mitigation. This template-based paradigm ensures symbolic interpretability by preventing hallucinations, offers superior edge efficiency with a compact architecture (i.e., occupies under 1GB of memory and runs at approximately 30 FPS on Raspberry Pi.), and supports multilingual adaptability without retraining. Initial results demonstrate promising performance for real-time, interpretable near-miss understanding and prediction, paving the way for proactive road safety interventions. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)},
