	abstract = {This chapter examines the challenges and solutions of integrating artificial intelligence (AI) into public governance, using Albania as a case study to illustrate current AI transparency and accountability frameworks. As emerging technologies become embedded in public services and decision-making process, governments face growing pressure to ensure transparency in the use of algorithmic systems. This chapter takes a two-fold approach: first, it analyzes the legal and policy frameworks for AI transparency and accountability, referencing EU and OECD standards as well as Albanian legislation, and second, it explores practical challenges such as limited data infrastructure, regulatory gaps, and the need for skilled personnel. With Albania making recent legal strides to align with EU standards, this chapter outlines relevant legal and policy instruments regulating AI systems. As AI becomes pervasive across sectors, there is a pressing need to understand its legal nature, determine applicable laws, and identify responsible institutions to ensure transparency and interpretability. This chapter also thoroughly examines the impact of AI on legal systems. It evaluates the interdisciplinary cooperation among data scientists, legal experts, and ethicists to successfully address legal and ethical issues that arise from the integration of AI in governance. © 2026 Eralda Methasani çani, Miralda çuka, Andrea Mazelliu. All rights reserved.},
