	abstract = {Climate change (CC) affects varying sectors of the Nigeria’s socio-economic development and sustainability with considerable threat particularly to the agricultural sector. However, the assessment of the potential impacts of CC in the country is hindered by poor data quality and inadequate climate monitoring infrastructure. This study reviews the increasing role of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in bridging these critical gaps in CC assessment. It uses a specialized search query to retrieve relevant articles from the ScienceDirect and IEEE Xplore platform using the systematic literature review (SLR) method. Selected articles include articles that feature AI methods such as machine learning, deep learning and geospatial technology in climate change impact assessment. Some of the identified applications of AI techniques in climate forecasting include in flood, drought, heatwave, wildfire, landslide, sea-level rise, and air quality predictions. The reviewed studies show that AI is able to bridge the gap on several pertinent challenges of CCI assessment in Nigeria and has led to significant improvement in drought and flood forecasting Limitations to AI deployment in CCI impact in Nigeria include data limitation, ethical concerns. and computational limitations. Despite these challenges, the study concludes that with strategic investments in ethical AI governance and incorporation of emerging technologies, AI can significantly improve Nigeria’s capacity to monitor and respond to CC impacts. © 2025 NIPES Pub.},
