	abstract = {This study presents an FPGA-accelerated AI-driven framework for real-time safety monitoring in industrial environments, incorporating advanced hardware-software co-optimization techniques such as hybrid precision quantization, channel pruning, and deterministic pipeline design. The proposed system achieves a millisecond-level response time, 95.2% detection accuracy, and energy consumption of 37.6 W, addressing the critical challenges of latency, accuracy, and power efficiency in safety-critical applications. Experimental validation using an eight-scenario dataset simulating real-world safety violations demonstrated the system's robustness, with an average false positive rate of 2.1%. Comparative analysis with Jetson TX2 and traditional FPGA solutions revealed a 4.7x acceleration in processing efficiency and a 67.5% reduction in power consumption, underscoring the advantages of the optimized architecture. Field deployment in a tobacco manufacturing environment confirmed the framework's industrial viability, achieving a 98.3% reduction in production line stoppages and maintaining a false trigger rate below 0.07%. These results establish the proposed system as a benchmark for real-time AI safety monitoring in dynamic industrial workflows.  © 2025 The Authors.},
