	abstract = {This chapter explores how agentic Artificial Intelligence (AI) is reshaping economic, social, and ethical structures. Unlike traditional automation, agentic AI autonomously adapts decision-making, replicating or surpassing human cognition. This shift induces a "phase change," transforming institutions, labor markets, and societal norms. While AI enhances efficiency, it exacerbates economic disparities, challenging GDP as a sole metric. We propose alternative indicators integrating well-being, equity, and sustainability. In business, AI-driven models create new data asymmetries, requiring adaptive governance. Trust, as both a relational and regulatory principle, is essential for balancing innovation and accountability. Advocating for Human-Centered AI, transparency, and fairness, this chapter underscores the need for interdisciplinary collaboration and robust data-sharing frameworks to ensure inclusive and equitable AI-driven progress. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing.},
