	abstract = {In the realm of e-commerce, accurately predicting sales and the success trajectory of newly launched cold-start products poses a significant challenge. This work presents a scalable AI framework developed for Flipkart, a leading Indian e-commerce platform, with the objective of identifying high-potential listings from a vast inventory of cold-start products. Employing a multimodal approach, our framework amalgamates product attributes such as price, type, and color with image embeddings derived from an EfficientNet deep learning model. Following this, we employ a boosting model to determine the potential scores of products, based on historical data like units sold, impressions, and product-page-views. For new products without historical data, the framework relies only on their attributes and images to estimate potential scores. A subset of listings with the highest predicted scores is then selected and prominently displayed to customers through search, merchandising, and recommendation channels. This strategic selection aims to identify products with high click-through rates, conversions, and overall demand, to enhance their discovery on the platform. Additionally, the methodology incorporates a multi-armed bandits strategy, enabling adaptation to temporal market changes and facilitating the creation of a feedback loop. Overall, this framework, while developed for Flipkart, offers the versatility to extend to other e-commerce platforms, enabling efficient screening of high-potential listings from a vast exploration space and effectively tackling the cold-start challenge in e-commerce. © 2025 Elsevier Ltd},
