	abstract = {This bibliometric analysis investigates post-millennial research on algorithmic fairness to extract insights, define the most influential research directions, identify research gaps, analyze research entry barriers, and discover growth patterns, collaboration patterns, and opportunities. Reliance on AI-powered algorithms in decision-making processes has directed substantial effort and interest toward algorithmic fairness. These advancements impact diverse fields such as technology and engineering, social justice, personal and public finance, and medicine, among many others. Motivated by the scarcity of recent bibliometric studies, this analysis covers the time period from 1 January 2000 to 31 December 2023; we identified 787 relevant research articles revealing the emerging nature of this niche research field, a compound growth pattern in interest and efforts, and no significant entry barriers concerning funding. The metadata is extracted from the Web of Science database and preprocessed using the pandas module. Then, the analyses facilitate the Web of Science-Analysis tools, the Bibliometrix package, and the VOSviewer. This study also highlights the research's geographical distribution and collaboration network to reveal key potential contributors to future endeavors. © 2025 Scrivener Publishing LLC. All rights reserved.},
