	abstract = {With the rapid growth of digital content and AI-generated information, the risk of misinformation has become increasingly prominent, leading to a pressing need for verification and authenticity checks across various forms of data. Ensuring the accuracy of information in various domains is crucial to maintaining public trust. Medical chatbots powered by large language models have demonstrated significant potential in providing healthcare-related information. However, the reliability of medical chatbots is paramount, especially in preventing misinformation and hallucinated responses. In this paper, we propose a novel multi-step verification framework to enhance the reliability of chatbot-generated medical responses. This approach is integrated into GeoSI to develop an intelligent interactive system that allows users to explore and summarize real-time medical information. The system combines Selenium, Bing Search, and OpenAI's mini API v4.0 for querying, with data verification from WHO and Medical-NER to refine responses and reduce hallucinations. Evaluated on the COVID-Fact dataset, our method achieves 79.5% accuracy, significantly improving chatbot reliability. Moreover, this multi-step verification and data integration strategy can also be applied to multimedia content analysis, particularly in detecting deepfake and cheapfake, supporting content authenticity verification. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s). Publication rights licensed to ACM.},
