	abstract = {The shift to a service economy has profoundly transformed Human Resource Management (HRM), emphasizing soft skills, flexibility, and customer-centric competencies. With the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and data-driven practices, HRM is undergoing strategic transformation, balancing technological advancements and human potential. AI-powered tools, such as chatbots and predictive analytics, streamline recruitment, talent management, and performance evaluation, enabling data-driven decision-making while improving efficiency and objectivity. Automation enhances operational processes, freeing HR professionals for strategic tasks and fostering a culture of continuous improvement. However, these advancements bring ethical challenges, including data privacy, bias in AI algorithms, and the risk of dehumanization in recruitment. The future of work, shaped by flexible and hybrid models, emphasizes employee well-being, mental health support, and personalized learning pathways. These trends highlight the dual role of AI: as an enabler of HR innovation and as a tool requiring human oversight to ensure fairness and alignment with organizational values. Overcoming challenges, such as upskilling HR professionals and implementing responsible AI principles, will be critical for leveraging AI's potential while preserving ethical integrity. This chapter explores the interplay of technology and human potential, showcasing examples and insights into the transformative role of HR in the service economy, alongside the need for strategic and ethical integration of AI in HR processes. © 2026 Pushan Kumar Dutta, Amarnath Padhi, Sulagna Das, Vinod Kr Sharma and Poshan Yu. All rights reserved.},
